# Statement section

Import WebFormat from "./web_format.lg".
Import WebProblem from "./web_problem.lg".

A problem's formal statements, fetched when the section appears: each a LOGOS
kernel document with its goal, its hash, how it was made and how its review
stands, the accepted one first.

## Component StatementSection (pid: Text)

State:
    Let rows be a new Seq of StatementRow.
    Let status be "loading".

Actions:
    When this component appears:
        Get "/api/v1/problem/statements?id=" + urlEncode(pid) as Seq of StatementRow, then arrived.

    To arrived (answer: Result of Seq of StatementRow and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (list):
                Set rows to list.
                Set status to "loaded".
            When Err (e):
                Set status to e's message.

View:
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Formal statements</h2>
      {for each s in rows, keyed by s's id:}
        <div class="statement">
          <div class="statement-head">
            <span class="chip review-{s's reviewState}">{s's reviewState}</span>
            <span class="chip">route {s's route}</span>
            <span class="chip kind">goal {s's goalName}</span>
            <span class="hash">sha256 {shortHash(s's sha256)}</span>
            <span class="entry-meta">{s's author} · {s's model} · {formatStamp(s's createdAt)}</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="doc">{s's document}</pre>
        </div>
      {else:}
        {if status is equal to "loaded":}
          <p class="empty" id="no-statements">No formal statement yet: the problem is waiting for a formalize unit.</p>
        {else:}
          <p class="empty">{status}</p>
        {end}
      {end}
    </div>
